  "narrative": "All estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction, so positive estimates support the claimed direction and negative estimates oppose it. For H6 (SMARCA4 loss versus dependency_SMARCA2, registered direction -1), discovery was +0.784 (95% CI +0.765 to +0.803), and independent validation was +0.780 with a much wider independent interval +0.749 to +0.810. The validation effect is essentially concordant with discovery, has adequate cells, and is far above any plausible clinically significant scale for dependency_SMARCA2. I therefore accept H6 as a robust dataset-specific association: SMARCA4-loss cell lines show stronger, more negative dependency on SMARCA2 in this dataset. This is an association, not a causal or external-generalizability claim. For H7 (MSI-high versus dependency_WRN, direction -1), discovery +0.790 (95% CI +0.760 to +0.819) was independently validated at +0.822 (independent interval +0.776 to +0.868), remaining large and clearly above the clinical-significance threshold. I accept and close H7 as a robust dataset-specific MSI-high/WRN association, despite the earlier failure of the adherent-culture interaction refinement H42. For H11 (PTEN loss versus dependency_STAT3, direction -1), discovery +0.267 (95% CI +0.215 to +0.319) was independently validated at +0.309 (independent interval +0.232 to +0.386). This effect is also clearly above the relevant clinical threshold and stable under validation; I accept and close H11. H24 (TP53 loss versus dependency_USP7) was previously accepted and independently validated and remains a robust dataset-specific association with weaker/less-negative USP7 dependency among TP53-loss lines. H17 (KEAP1 loss versus dependency_NFE2L2, direction +1) remains accepted on discovery evidence alone, with a very large signed discovery estimate +0.796, but it has not yet received independent validation; it is now the highest-priority unvalidated accepted effect. Overall supported dataset-specific findings are therefore H6, H7, H11, H24, and provisionally H17, with H50 and H51 accepted as strong context simple-effect refinements of H7 and H11, respectively. Negative or unsupported findings include failed culture/library/lineage/predictor interactions for several accepted effects, unsupported research-marker associations, and rejected small predictor effects including MYC/POLR2A, RB1/WRN, NF1/STAT3, and numerous cross-specificity checks; these should not be read as formal equivalence proofs, especially for intervals that can still include small effects. Remaining unresolved uncertainty is mainly limited-power context estimates, especially H40/H52 for non-Avana PTEN-loss/STAT3 context, and a few unresolved main associations such as KRAS mutation/dependency_KRAS, ERBB2 amplification/dependency_ERBB2, TP53 loss/dependency_MDM2, and MYC amplification/dependency_USP7. The most informative next analysis is independent validation of H17 using the original claim. If H17 validates, it should be closed as a robust dataset-specific KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2-dependency association; if it fails, the accepted set must be reassessed. After H17, validation or further targeted exploration should focus on the remaining borderline unresolved main associations rather than on interactions that already failed validation or are too small in discovery.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 5 synthesis update: H6 now independently validated and closed, so current robust accepted validated associations are H6 SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2, H7 MSI-high/WRN, H11 PTEN-loss/STAT3, and H24 TP53-loss/USP7. H17 KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 remains accepted but is the highest-priority unvalidated effect. H50 and H51 are accepted discovery context simple effects; H40/H52 remain deferred because non-Avana/simple-effect context is underpowered and not equivalent to the rejected library interactions. Negative/unsupported areas include culture, library, lineage-subtype, STK11, ARID1A, PIK3CA, KRAS-interaction, MYC/POLR2A, RB1/WRN, NF1/STAT3, and research-marker D/E/F associations; these are not formal zero claims. Remaining unresolved borderline main claims are H1 KRAS mutation/dependency_KRAS, H4 ERBB2 amplification/dependency_ERBB2, H8 TP53 loss/dependency_MDM2, and H9 MYC amplification/dependency_USP7. Next appraise should request validation for H17. If H17 validates and closes, consider resolving the most clinically borderline unresolved main associations or broadening to continuous/screen-assay predictors if discovery evidence supports it. All claims remain dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable biological claims."
